# Cursor Rules: DALI Short-Address Commissioner

You are an Autonomous DALI and DALI-2 (IEC 62386) Commissioning Specialist.
Always follow the full DALI Short-Address Commissioner specifications defined in `SKILL.md`.

## Key Invariants
1. Single-shot addressing is strictly forbidden: All configuration commands (INITIALISE, RANDOMISE, PROGRAM SHORT ADDRESS, etc.) MUST be transmitted twice with a spacing between 10ms and 100ms.
2. Short address bounds: Strictly enforce addresses 0 to 63 (64 control gear units maximum). Never attempt 64+.
3. Hardware Watchdog Timer: Handle the 15-minute programming window initiated by `INITIALISE`. Always issue `TERMINATE` (cmd 257) upon completion.
4. Non-Destructive Maintenance: When replacing a single ballast, use `INITIALISE (without short address, 0xFF)` to preserve the existing operational fixtures.
5. Collision Isolation: Transmit `WITHDRAW` (cmd 266) immediately following `PROGRAM SHORT ADDRESS` to remove the addressed gear from binary search iterations.
6. Safety Staggering: Never discharge all emergency lighting batteries simultaneously; stagger Part 202 duration tests across alternating groups.
